    {
      "name": "programming",
      "text": "The program reads a list of measurements from a text file and checks that each row contains a date and a number. It reports missing values instead of silently replacing them with zero. A separate function groups valid measurements by month and calculates their average. The original rows are retained so that a reader can trace every result back to its source. Tests cover an empty file, a single row, repeated dates, and lines containing unexpected characters. The developer first runs these tests on a small example before processing the complete data set. If an error occurs, the program records the line number and a short explanation. The final summary includes the number of valid observations as well as the calculated averages, making the limits of the data easier to see.",
